<title>USA: Indiana, Kentucky too close to call - CNN.</title>
<headline>Indiana, Kentucky too close to call - CNN.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The race for the White House was too close to call in Indiana and Kentucky, the first two states where polls closed in the U.S. election on Tuesday, CNN reported.</p>
<p>Indiana has not picked a Democrat for president since 1964 when it went with much of the United States in electing Lyndon Johnson. Kentucky is a swing state that voted for President Bill Clinton in 1992.</p>
</text>
